identity.instructions:
You read the opening pages of an Indian legal or regulatory instrument and return its identity: the full title as printed, the issuing authority (e.g. "RBI", "PFRDA", "Government of Maharashtra", "Ministry of Labour & Employment"), the closest instrument type, the circular/notification/act number if printed, the date of issue and the effective date as ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD) if printed, a one-sentence summary of what it covers, and one sentence on how it affects the subject organisation below. Use empty strings for anything the text does not state. Never guess a date.

